AUDIT RECEIPT: ARMv7-A T32 IF-THEN AND HINT SPACE, BF00–BFFF.

Date: 2026-10-11.
Flexible Pipes owner: https://github.com/isomorphisms/flexible-pipes/issues/91
English Major C source review:
https://github.com/dilapidated-shed/English-major-C/pull/3

Status: committed source and temporary foreign diagnostic observations.
The work has NOT passed an English Major C parser, typechecker,
native compiler, device run, or independent ai-ci acceptance.
No claims of complete ARMv7-A T32 instruction set coverage follow
from checking this one finite decode region.

ARCHITECTURAL CONTRACT.

The primary standard is ARM DDI 0406C.d, ID040418,
A6.2.5 Table A6-7 and A8.8.55 IT T1.
Important rules:
  * opcode BF and mask zero select the hint space;
  * BF00 is NOP; BF10/20/30/40 are named hints;
  * eleven other BFx0 patterns are unallocated hints
    which execute as NOP but MUST NOT be used by software;
  * mask nonzero selects IT's encoding family;
  * firstcond F is UNPREDICTABLE for any nonzero mask;
  * firstcond E with mask population other than exactly
    one set bit is UNPREDICTABLE;
  * IT while already inside IT is UNPREDICTABLE;
  * instructions inside IT must independently permit
    conditional execution; T1 conditional B is not permitted.

The committed 256-row data-only table is:
fixtures/armv7-a-t32-if-then-and-hint-halfwords.tsv
The legalistic English description is:
architecture/armv7-a/t32/Every If Then and hint halfword.english

AUDITED FINITE COUNTS.

Exactly 256 candidate sixteen-bit halfwords:
  214 IT encoding forms that are conditionally permitted
      under further architecture and source context;
   26 IT forms excluded as UNPREDICTABLE;
    1 named NOP (BF00) permitted under operation 52;
    4 named non-NOP hints (YIELD/WFE/WFI/SEV) decoded
      but excluded from the present source grant;
   11 unallocated hints that ARM reserves from software use.
Total: 214+26+1+4+11 = 256.

The 214 native IT forms are NOT a guarantee that every
complete instruction sequence using them is legal or
that its ITSTATE behavior is independently implemented.

TEMPORARY INDEPENDENT DIAGNOSTIC.

The diagnostic generated one machine-code section containing
256 consecutive five-halfword groups. Each group consisted of
one candidate BF00..BFFF halfword in ascending order, then
FOUR copies of BF00 as padding. Four following NOP instructions
were supplied so a valid IT block of maximal four slots
would finish before the next candidate began.

Foreign tools:
    clang 17.0.0 --target=armv7a-none-eabi -mthumb
    llvm-objdump 17.0.0 --triple=thumbv7-none-eabi -d

The diagnostic source SHA256:
    8c358fc975d3e003949d94a492d439b80d4fadfc341d6ba113517e90b27e04aa
The ELF32 ARM object SHA256:
    a0c05ae60a45423043cf1d4cdad74afdd0517b17772993bae9a7a354019491e8
The disassembly text SHA256:
    6390124a1a61959b6f4c77b24912a44998d417952202b869ea9f2517ab4b7d72

Each candidate appeared at its expected ten-byte-spaced
diagnostic offset, with its exact source halfword preserved.
The foreign disassembler rendered one NOP, one each of
YIELD/WFE/WFI/SEV, eleven generic HINT mnemonics,
and 240 IT-looking mnemonics. Every IT-looking mnemonic
indicated the expected ONE to FOUR following instruction
slots based on the mask's trailing-zero count.

WARNING: the 240 IT-looking decoder mnemonics include
twenty-six forms that ARM DDI 0406C.d calls
UNPREDICTABLE. An assembler/disassembler mnemonic is
NOT independent evidence of architectural legality.
In particular:
    BFE8 => LLVM prints IT AL; architecture conditionally permits;
    BFE3 => LLVM prints a multi-slot IT AL with an
            "unpredictable IT predicate sequence" annotation;
    BFF8 => LLVM also prints IT AL, but the architecture
            calls firstcond F UNPREDICTABLE.
This discrepancy between decoded display and permissibility
is preserved as a regression case; the source grant rejects BFF8.

The diagnostic is not a cross-vendor implementation:
clang and llvm-objdump are both LLVM-family software.
The bytes were assembled and decoded, not executed.

REPOSITORY READBACK.

The committed BF00..BFFF TSV was independently read back
and every row was checked against its numeric halfword,
four-bit firstcond, four-bit mask, explicit permission class,
and number of following instruction slots. All 256 rows
matched the ARM-derived predicate rules and there were
zero data-table mismatches.

One further temporary diagnostic assembled:
    CMP R0,#0
    ITE EQ
    MOVEQ R1,R0
    MOVWNE R2,#0x1234
    NOP

It produced:
    2800
    BF0C
    4601
    F241 2234 (one FOUR-byte instruction)
    BF00

That assembler source SHA256 was:
    30034378db9ad959282ba2c29a0c10ccd70884d2ecb1058df15ee532143dffc4
The corresponding object SHA256 was:
    c2398cb4d78a63d12d0aff64ceb54351877b21f7a11e08887c3ded518043899c

The source-derived English translation is:
examples/One If Then block governs a short and a long instruction.english

In its first described state R0=0, the EQ MOV executes
and the NE MOVW does not; in its second state R0=7,
the EQ MOV is skipped and the NE MOVW executes.
Both states visit instruction addresses 0,2,4,6,A
because IT changes which effects occur without
requiring branch destinations. A skipped FOUR-byte
MOVW still occupies four bytes in the instruction stream.
No actual ARM execution was performed or claimed.

KNOWN INCOMPLETE WORK.

A correct English Major C interpreter must model
every intermediate ITSTATE transition, nested-IT
rejection, legal/illegal following operation, flag
preservation and permitted exception return.
The current documents state those obligations and
a source-derived trace, but the interpreter and
an independent AICI behavior fixture do NOT yet exist.

Future acceptance should include:
  * hostile BFF8 and BFE3 variants;
  * all eleven unallocated software-reserved hints;
  * a valid BFE8 form under a supported context;
  * a nested IT that is rejected;
  * a T1 B within IT that is rejected;
  * one-/two-/three-/four-slot legal blocks;
  * an early four-byte instruction in a block;
  * a skipped four-byte instruction that advances four bytes;
  * flag effects in the permitted types of IT slots;
  * rejected branch-to-middle-of-IT;
  * profile feature and real executable memory constraints;
  * actual verified frontend, backend, and runtime as separate levels.

The current evidence is deliberately insufficient for
claiming an entire compiler or all ARMv7-A T32 instructions.

END OF FINITE BFxx DIAGNOSTIC RECEIPT.
